A fast, no-bake alternative to traditional scalloped potatoes cooked entirely on the stovetop in a single skillet. Rich, creamy, and topped with melted sharp cheddar.

*Adapted from [Rachel Cooks](https://www.rachelcooks.com/stovetop-scalloped-potatoes/#wprm-recipe-container-35071).*

## Ingredients

- 1 tablespoon unsalted butter
- 2 pounds potatoes, thinly sliced (about ⅛-inch slices)
- ½ medium onion, thinly sliced into half-moons
- ¾ cup reduced-sodium chicken broth (or vegetable broth)
- ½ cup heavy cream
- ½ teaspoon kosher salt
- ¼ teaspoon coarse ground black pepper
- Pinch freshly grated nutmeg (or ground nutmeg)
- 1 ¼ cups shredded sharp cheddar cheese
- Fresh chives, chopped for garnish (optional)

## Instructions

1. **Sauté the Potatoes and Onions:** In a large skillet with a lid, melt the butter over medium heat. Add sliced potatoes and onions. Cook, stirring frequently, for about 5 minutes to begin softening.
2. **Mix the Cream Mixture:** In a large measuring cup or bowl, whisk together chicken broth, heavy cream, salt, pepper, and nutmeg.
3. **Simmer Until Tender:** Pour the liquid over the potatoes and onions. Increase heat to medium-high and bring to a boil. Reduce heat to medium-low, cover with the lid, and simmer for 13 to 15 minutes until the potatoes are fork-tender and the sauce starts to thicken.
4. **Melt the Cheese:** Sprinkle the shredded cheddar cheese evenly over the potatoes. Cover the pan and cook for 2 to 3 minutes until the cheese is completely melted.
5. **Optional Broil:** If you cooked in a cast iron or oven-safe skillet, pop it under the broiler on high for 2 to 3 minutes until bubbling and golden brown.
6. **Rest and Garnish:** Let stand for 5 to 10 minutes off heat so the sauce thickens into a rich gravy. Garnish with fresh chopped chives and serve warm.

## Notes

- **Potato Variety:** Yukon Golds or Russets work best. Yukon Golds hold their shape and have a buttery texture, while Russets break down slightly to create an even thicker sauce.
- **Mandoline Slicer:** A mandoline makes quick, even ⅛-inch slices so all potatoes cook at the same rate.
